Subject: server: drop VMS privileges once the listeners are bound

On Unix, lighttpd binds its listening sockets as root and then switches to
server.username.  OpenVMS has no root: VMS TCP/IP lets only processes with
SYSPRV, OPER or BYPASS bind ports below 1024 (probes/r_bindpriv.c).  The kit
installs LIGHTTPD.EXE with /PRIVILEGED=OPER and runs it under an account
with only TMPMBX and NETMBX (docs/DECISIONS.md D12).

Right after network_init() has bound the listeners, disable every privilege
for the rest of the process's life and keep TMPMBX and NETMBX
(vmsport/vms_privs.c).  Logged, so the error log shows the drop happened;
a failure stops the server rather than leaving it privileged.

--- a/src/server.c
+++ b/src/server.c
@@ -1801,6 +1801,20 @@
 		return -1;
 	}
 	srv->stdin_fd = -1;
+  #ifdef __VMS
+	/* ports < 1024 needed OPER (installed-image privilege): drop it */
+	{
+		extern unsigned int vms_drop_privileges(void);
+		const unsigned int vst = vms_drop_privileges();
+		if (0 != vst) {
+			log_error(srv->errh, __FILE__, __LINE__,
+			  "VMS: could not drop privileges (status %%X%08X)", vst);
+			return -1;
+		}
+		log_error(srv->errh, __FILE__, __LINE__,
+		  "VMS: listeners bound; privileges now TMPMBX,NETMBX");
+	}
+  #endif
 
 	if (i_am_root) {
 #ifdef HAVE_PWD_H
